<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Puno Region</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Department of Puno</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puno">Puno</a> Region is a region of south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a> on the border with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bolivia">Bolivia</a>, covering the northern and western shores of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-titicaca">Lake Titicaca</a> and the high Altiplano. It was home to Pukará and later to the Colla and Lupaca kingdoms, and as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a> of Puno it joined the South Peruvian Republic in 1836. Its capital is the city of Puno.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/puno-region.jpg" alt="Puno Region" width="320" height="235" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Incacity · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Isla_Suasi_PUNO-PERU.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
